      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hi, I'm currently analyzing some sensor data from the new roundabout installation on the south side of the city. The throughput looks mostly efficient, but we're seeing some really strange, non-linear fluctuations in the vehicle exit rates during the transition from off-peak to peak hours. \n\nActually, it's more than just fluctuations; there seem to be these brief, irregular patterns of movement that don't quite align with our standard kinematic wave models. It's almost as if there's an unaccounted-for disturbance causing the flow to briefly become erratic or \"stutter\" before stabilizing again. From a traffic modeling perspective, how would you characterize these kinds of unexplained irregularities or sudden, localized disturbances in a high-density flow system?",
